##================= /etc/anon/anonrc -- local/anyone, A's side ===============##
#
# The PAYER's way onto the network: a SOCKS5 proxy and nothing else. This opens
# no ORPort and publishes no service. It is what the toon client's `socksProxy`
# / `TOON_SOCKS` names, and the only route it has to the connector.
#
# Mounted READ-ONLY at /etc/anon/anonrc.

# WITHOUT THIS THE DAEMON DOES NOT START. `anon` refuses to run until its terms
# are accepted and, in a non-interactive container, FAILS FAST rather than
# prompting: "User has not agreed to the terms and conditions. Exiting." It is
# the most common reason a first bring-up leaves a container that exited
# immediately beside a connector that looks healthy and is unreachable.
AgreeToTerms 1

User anond
DataDirectory /var/lib/anon

# EXPLICIT, and it cannot be dropped: the image's entrypoint appends a
# `Nickname` when it finds none, and this file is mounted read-only, so a
# missing one is a write failure at boot rather than a default.
Nickname toonlocalanyoneA

ClientOnly 1
ORPort 0
DirPort 0
ControlSocket 0

# Bound to 0.0.0.0 so the payer's container can reach it; the network it sits on
# holds nothing else, and the policy below is the belt to that braces.
SocksPort 0.0.0.0:9050
SocksPolicy accept 10.0.0.0/8
SocksPolicy accept 172.16.0.0/12
SocksPolicy accept 192.168.0.0/16
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.0/8
SocksPolicy reject *

Log notice stdout
Log notice file /var/lib/anon/notice.log
